# usa-wa#389 — earlyoom on a 7.7 GiB host with NO swap that runs the production
# usa-wa service alongside interactive agent sessions.
#
# Why it exists here at all: with no swap, the kernel past its memory ceiling
# does not reliably kill anything — it fails atomic allocations in unrelated
# processes (tailscaled, ksoftirqd) while the production service starves. That is
# how CannObserv/broker's 2026-09-16 outage presented, nothing OOM-killed and the
# bus down 57m 48s (gregoryfoster/skills#295). earlyoom acts *before* the kernel
# reaches that state.
#
# -r 3600: hourly memory report (the packaged default; keeps the journal quiet).
# -m/-s are left at their defaults (10% / 10%, SIGKILL at 5%). With zero swap the
# swap condition is permanently satisfied (0 <= 10%), so the memory threshold
# alone governs — intended here, and worth saying, because the documented "both
# must be below minimum" reads as though it would never fire.
#
# --prefer: the SocratiCode MCP servers and any npm install a launch performs are
# the spikes on this host. Measured 2026-09-19: three concurrent `node …
# .npm/_npx/…/socraticode` servers at oom_score 676-679 against usa-wa's 668 —
# i.e. the cause and the victim were within noise of each other.
#
# --avoid: `uv` is the serving unit's process name. ExecStart is `uv run …
# uvicorn`, so the comm the kernel and earlyoom see is `uv`, NOT `uvicorn` — a
# regex written for the name this repo calls that process everywhere else would
# protect nothing and read as though it did. Both are listed, and
# scripts/tests/test_memory_protection.py EXECUTES these regexes against `uv` so
# the trap cannot come back. postgres already ships at oom_score_adj -900 from
# the Debian packaging and needs nothing here, but is listed so a future
# repackaging cannot quietly remove that protection.
#
# systemd's ExecStart is `/usr/bin/earlyoom $EARLYOOM_ARGS`. Verified on this
# host that the single quotes below are consumed rather than passed through:
# /proc/<pid>/cmdline reads `--prefer` `^(node|npm|esbuild)$`, unquoted.
#
# Install: sudo cp deploy/default/earlyoom /etc/default/earlyoom && sudo systemctl restart earlyoom
# Verify:  tr '\0' '\n' < /proc/$(systemctl show earlyoom -p MainPID --value)/cmdline
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 3600 --prefer '^(node|npm|esbuild)$' --avoid '^(uv|uvicorn|postgres|sshd|systemd|dockerd|tailscaled)$'"
